/-!
# The avx2_x8 body of a later pass, residue 16

The 208 body slices `K2 .. K210` of a second or later pass: the cuts are stripped of the 40
spilled cells (`stripK8 16`), which the symbolic memory `m8P 16` serves from its push list;
the first two cuts carry the loop-carried vector registers (`KHs 16`, `KH3s 16`;
`Avx2X8WStrip.stripFacts 16`: `sliceV2s`, `sliceV3s`).  `bodyS_runW` composes them from the stripped
invariant head to the stripped `K210` (generated by `tools/avx_x8w.py`).
-/
namespace Hashtree.Proofs.Avx2X8WBodyR16S

/-- The two replayed head cuts, read off the residue's kernel check. -/
theorem sliceV2s : sliceCheck prog 4 (m8P 16) orcB 8 (KHs 16) (KH3s 16) T2 = true :=
  (stripFacts 16 stripOk_16).2.1
theorem sliceV3s : sliceCheck prog 4 (m8P 16) orcB 8 (KH3s 16) (stripK8 16 K4) T3 = true :=
  (stripFacts 16 stripOk_16).2.2.1

